  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lead">This site collects nothing about you.</p>
  <section><h2>No cookies, no analytics</h2><p>The site sets no cookies and runs no analytics, tracking or advertising code, unless you choose to sign in with GitHub (see <a href="#github">Signing in with GitHub</a>). There is no cookie banner because nothing here needs your consent.</p></section>
  <section><h2>No requests to other sites</h2><p>Every page, font, image and demo is served from this site. Pages make no requests to other services. The one exception is the editors at /editor/app/, which talk to GitHub (api.github.com) only after you sign in. Links to GitHub and other sites are only followed when you choose them.</p></section>
  <section><h2>No accounts or forms</h2><p>Automata has no accounts and the site has no forms. Search runs in your browser and sends nothing. If you want your games kept on all your devices, you can sign in with your own GitHub account.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Your browser's storage</h2><p>The site itself stores nothing in your browser. If you start an embedded demo, the demo may keep its game state in this browser's local storage. The editors at /editor/app/ keep the games you make, and the words you type into them, in this browser's private storage and send them nowhere. Save a copy of a game to keep it somewhere else. That data stays on your device; clear it by clearing this site's data in your browser. The examples' live preview can't use your browser's storage, and an edit you make to an example lives only in the page's address.</p></section>
  <section id="github"><h2>Signing in with GitHub</h2><p>Signing in is optional and free, and it keeps your games in your own GitHub account, not with us. When you press Sign in with GitHub, you go to GitHub, say yes there, and come back. A small function on this site, which stores nothing and logs nothing, passes GitHub's answers along because GitHub needs a secret that a web page cannot hold.</p><p>Two cookies are involved, both only on /api/github/, both unreadable to the page and to anyone but this site. <code>af_gh_start</code> lasts ten minutes, while you are on GitHub's page. <code>af_gh</code> holds your sign-in in encrypted form, so you stay signed in; it is removed when you sign out, and is otherwise good for about six months. Your access token stays in the page's memory and is never written to your browser's storage or to an address.</p><p>Your games go from your browser straight to your own repository on GitHub. They do not pass through this site, and Automata keeps nothing. To stop, press Sign out in the editors, or remove Automata at github.com/settings/applications.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Hosting</h2><p>The site is static files. Like any web server, the host that serves them receives the standard request details: your IP address, the page requested and your browser's user agent. Automata adds no tracking on top of that.</p></section>
